{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Has acted treacherously</b> — The holy one is HaShem, who is a father to Israel with sons and daughters, as written: 'of His sons and daughters.'" "<b>And has married</b> — from the root of <b>כי יבעל בחור בתולה</b> (when a young man marries a virgin)." "<b>Daughter of a foreign god</b> — a servant of idolatry. And the meaning is that she is not from one father and one El."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:14.059199104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}